andrew@exicom.OZ.AU (Andrew Koschier) publicly declared:
>To use a unicorn apply it, but make sure it is not cursed first.
>Unicorn horns will cure blindness, confusion, stun, halluc(i think) sickenss,
>and restore lost stats.
>
>I consider a unicorn horn (uncursed) essential to negotiating the lower levels
>where you meet nasties that confuse/etc you.

I prefer a blessed unicorn horn.  It will cure you of everything at
once, instead of one application each for sickness, blindness, etc.
Besides, if it gets cursed by a Lich a blessed horn moves to "uncursed"
status and is still useful.

Cursed unicorn horns are also useful.  They *cause* all the things that
an uncursed horn cures.  Why would you want to do that?  It's a *great*
way to get confused before reading certain scrolls...  Just don't try
it without an uncursed horn on hand to cure you of the sickness and
other nasties you'll be hit with before you actually get confused!

BTW, the new #adjust command is wonderful.  My blessed unicorn horn is
always 'u', and the cursed horn is 'U'.  And the bag of holding is 'h',
the blindfold is 'b', the lockpick is 'l'...

Does the blessed/uncursed/cursed status of a lockpick matter?  Dunbarr
the Barbarian has been wandering around the entire game (I'm now in the
upper levels of hell) using a cursed lockpick.  There have been no
locks I haven't been able to open, and I haven't set off an abnormal
number of traps.

